Primary Key VS UNIQUE:

DEFINATION ::==> Primary key is mainly used to uniquely identify each row,
whereas a UNIQUE constraint is used to enforce uniqueness on one or more columns such as email, mobile number or username.
A table can have only one primary-key constraint but can have multiple UNIQUE constraints.


Primary Key :=>
Table ki row ko uniquely identify karti hai.
Duplicate nahi ho sakti.
NULL nahi ho sakti.
Ek table me normally one primary key constraint hota hai, although composite primary key me multiple columns ho sakte hain.

| Primary Key                        | UNIQUE                                    |
| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Row ko uniquely identify karti hai | Column/value uniqueness enforce karti hai |
| Duplicate ❌                        | Duplicate ❌                               |
| NULL ❌                             | NULL handling DBMS-specific hoti hai      |
| Table me one PK constraint         | Multiple UNIQUE constraints ho sakte hain |
| Usually identifier like `id`       | Email, mobile, username etc.              |


