Database Index
Interviewer:
“Database index kya hota hai? Why do we use indexes? What are their disadvantages?”

Simple samajh

Database index ko tu book ke index jaisa samajh.
Agar 500-page ki book me tujhe “Spring Boot” topic dhundhna hai aur index nahi hai, to page-by-page search karna padega.
Lekin agar book ke last me index hai:
Spring Boot → Page 245
to directly page 245 par ja sakta hai.
Database me bhi same concept hai.

Suppose users table:

SELECT *
FROM users
WHERE email = 'jigar@gmail.com';

Agar email par index nahi hai, database ko potentially bahut saare rows scan karne pad sakte hain.
Agar email par index hai, database efficiently matching row locate kar sakta hai.

🎯 Interview me bol:

“An index is a database data structure used to improve the performance of data retrieval operations. It helps the
database find rows faster instead of scanning the entire table. Indexes are commonly created on columns that
are frequently used in WHERE, JOIN, ORDER BY or sometimes GROUP BY conditions.”


Then interviewer agar pooche “disadvantage?”
Bol:
“The main disadvantage is that indexes consume additional storage, and INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE operations can
become slightly slower because the database also needs to maintain the index whenever the indexed data changes.”

⭐ One-line example
CREATE INDEX idx_user_email ON users(email);

Ab:
SELECT *
FROM users
WHERE email = 'jigar@gmail.com';

email index ka benefit le sakti hai.


========================================================================================================================

Primary Key vs Index — Important

Ye confusion interview me ho sakta hai.

Primary Key automatically indexed hoti hai in most relational databases, but index aur primary key same cheez nahi hain.

Primary Key → row ko uniquely identify karne ke liye constraint.
Index → data retrieval ko fast karne ke liye structure.
Ek table me multiple indexes ho sakte hain.
Har indexed column necessarily unique nahi hota.

Example:

CREATE INDEX idx_city
ON users(city);

Agar 10,000 users Bangalore se hain, tab bhi city par normal index ho sakta hai.

⚠️ Interview trap

Interviewer:

“Should we create indexes on every column?”

❌ Never say yes.

Bol:

“No. We should create indexes selectively on columns that are frequently used for searching, joining, sorting or filtering. Too many indexes increase storage usage and can slow down write operations such as INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE.”

🧠 Yaad rakhne ka formula

INDEX = Fast Read ⚡ + Extra Storage 💾 + Slower Write ✍️

Ye line yaad rakh bhai. Interview me kaam aayegi.

