JOINs
Interviewer:

“What is a JOIN? Explain different types of JOINs with examples.”

Ye bahut important hai, especially Java/Spring Boot backend role ke liye.

Simple samajh

JOIN ka use multiple tables se related data combine karne ke liye hota hai.

Example:

employees

id	name	dept_id
1	Jigar	10
2	Rahul	20
3	Amit	30

departments

id	department
10	IT
20	HR
40	Finance
1️⃣ INNER JOIN

Sirf matching records deta hai.

SELECT e.name, d.department
FROM employees e
INNER JOIN departments d
ON e.dept_id = d.id;

Result:

Jigar  → IT
Rahul  → HR

Amit ka dept_id = 30 hai, matching department nahi hai, isliye nahi aayega.

2️⃣ LEFT JOIN

Left table ke saare records + matching right table records.

SELECT e.name, d.department
FROM employees e
LEFT JOIN departments d
ON e.dept_id = d.id;

Result:

Jigar  → IT
Rahul  → HR
Amit   → NULL
3️⃣ RIGHT JOIN

Right table ke saare records + matching left table records.

SELECT e.name, d.department
FROM employees e
RIGHT JOIN departments d
ON e.dept_id = d.id;

Result me Finance bhi aayega:

Jigar  → IT
Rahul  → HR
Amit   → NULL
NULL   → Finance
4️⃣ FULL OUTER JOIN

Dono tables ke saare records.

Matching ho to combine, otherwise NULL.

Conceptually:

LEFT JOIN + RIGHT JOIN

⚠️ MySQL me FULL OUTER JOIN directly supported nahi hai; usually LEFT JOIN + UNION se achieve kiya jaata hai.

🎯 Interview me bol

“JOIN is used to combine data from two or more tables based on a related column. The commonly used joins are
INNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN and FULL OUTER JOIN. INNER JOIN returns only matching records,
 while LEFT JOIN returns all records from the left table and matching records from the right table.”

Agar interviewer specifically pooche “Most commonly used JOIN?”

Bol:

“In real-world applications, INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN are probably the most commonly used.
For example, LEFT JOIN is useful when we want all customers even if some customers don't have related orders.”

🧠 Shortcut
INNER → Matching only
LEFT  → Everything from LEFT
RIGHT → Everything from RIGHT
FULL  → Everything from BOTH


