Subquery vs JOIN

Neither is always better. It depends on the query, data size, indexes and execution plan.
JOINs are generally a natural choice when we need to combine related tables,
while subqueries can make certain filtering or existence checks simpler.
 I would check the execution plan when performance is important.”


| Subquery                                           | JOIN                                               |
| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| Query ke andar query                               | Multiple tables ko combine karta hai               |
| Complex filtering me useful                        | Related data retrieve karne me useful              |
| Readability kabhi-kabhi better                     | Multiple tables ke data ke liye natural            |
| Performance case-dependent                         | Often efficient for relational data                |
| `WHERE`, `SELECT`, `FROM` etc. me use ho sakti hai | `ON` condition ke through tables connect karta hai |


=======================================================================================================================
Normal Subquery  vs Correlated Subquery

Normal Subquery:
Independent Query → Result → Outer Query

Correlated Subquery:
Outer Row → Inner Query → Result
Outer Next Row → Inner Query → Result

| Normal Subquery                         | Correlated Subquery                                    |
| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Outer query se independent ho sakti hai | Outer query par depend karti hai                       |
| Generally once evaluate ho sakti hai    | Conceptually outer rows ke according evaluate hoti hai |
| Outer query ka reference zaroori nahi   | Outer query ka reference hota hai                      |


