What is Database Normalization?

Simple definition :
Normalization is the process of organizing data in database tables to reduce data redundancy and avoid data inconsistency.

Simple words me:
Same information ko unnecessarily baar-baar store nahi karna aur data ko logically separate tables me organize karna.

========================================================================================================================

What is Database Normalization?

Jo information repeat ho rahi hai, usko properly separate tables me rakhna.


==========================>
1NF — Ek cell me ek value :

| Employee | Skills                 |
| -------- | ---------------------- |
| Jigar    | Java, Spring Boot, SQL |

Ek cell me 3 skills hain.

| Employee | Skill       |
| -------- | ----------- |
| Jigar    | Java        |
| Jigar    | Spring Boot |
| Jigar    | SQL         |


Yaad rakh:
1NF = One cell → One value



===========================>

2NF — Data ko unnecessarily repeat mat karo

| Employee | Project | Employee Name | Project Name |
| -------- | ------- | ------------- | ------------ |
| 1        | 101     | Jigar         | ERP          |
| 1        | 102     | Jigar         | Inventory    |

Yahan Jigar baar-baar aa raha hai.

Aur agar same employee 10 projects par hai:

Jigar
Jigar
Jigar
Jigar
...

To employee ki information alag table me rakh sakte hain.

Employee table
| employee_id | employee_name |
| ----------- | ------------- |
| 1           | Jigar         |


Project table
| project_id | project_name |
| ---------- | ------------ |
| 101        | ERP          |
| 102        | Inventory    |


Aur ek mapping table:

Employee_Project
| employee_id | project_id |
| ----------- | ---------- |
| 1           | 101        |
| 1           | 102        |


Yaad rakh:

2NF = Jo data kisi ek cheez ka hai, usko usi ke table me rakho.

Interview terminology: No partial dependency.

Lekin abhi interview me bas itna concept clear rakhna enough hai.


=====================>

3NF — Indirect information ko separate karo

Maan le:

| Employee ID | Employee Name | Department ID | Department Name |
| ----------- | ------------- | ------------- | --------------- |
| 1           | Jigar         | 10            | IT              |
| 2           | Amit          | 10            | IT              |

Ab dekho:
Employee ID → Department ID

Lekin:
Department ID → Department Name

Matlab Department Name directly employee se nahi, Department se related hai.
To separate kar do:

Employee
| Employee ID | Employee Name | Department ID |
| ----------- | ------------- | ------------- |
| 1           | Jigar         | 10            |
| 2           | Amit          | 10            |


Department
| Department ID | Department Name |
| ------------- | --------------- |
| 10            | IT              |

Ab agar IT ka naam change karna hai, sirf ek jagah update karna hai.

Yaad rakh:
3NF = Indirectly related data ko separate karo.

Technical interview line: No transitive dependency.

*****************************************
Teeno ko ekdum simple trick se yaad kar

1NF → Ek cell me ek value
2NF → Data unnecessarily repeat mat karo
3NF → Indirectly related data ko separate karo

Ya technical language:

1NF → Atomic values
2NF → No Partial Dependency
3NF → No Transitive Dependency
**************************************

Interview me short answer

Agar interviewer bole "Explain normalization", tu ye bol:

“Normalization is used to organize database data properly and reduce duplicate data.
 In 1NF, each cell contains a single value. In 2NF, we remove partial dependency and keep data related to the correct entity.
 In 3NF, we remove indirect or transitive dependency by separating related information into different tables.”


